---
import CatalogueHeader from "../../../components/v2-catalogue/CatalogueHeader.astro";
import DataBenchmarkEvidence from "../../../components/v2-data/DataBenchmarkEvidence.astro";
import DataCompatibilityEvidence from "../../../components/v2-data/DataCompatibilityEvidence.astro";
import DataRuntimeTelemetry from "../../../components/v2-data/DataRuntimeTelemetry.astro";
import DataEvidenceStates from "../../../components/v2-data/DataEvidenceStates.astro";
import {
  dataVisualisationFixtureNotice,
  dataVisualisationSummary
} from "../../../lib/v2-data-visualisation.mjs";
import "../../../../../src/v2.css";
import "../../../../../src/v2/data-visualisation.css";
import "../../../../../src/theme.js";
import "../../../styles/v2-lab.css";
import "../../../styles/v2-calm-lab.css";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const basePath = base.endsWith("/") ? base : `${base}/`;
const pageUrl = new URL(`${basePath}v2/data/`, Astro.site);
const socialImage = new URL(`${basePath}og/cards/visual-language.jpg`, Astro.site);
const catalogueUrl = `${basePath}v2/`;
const guideUrl = `${basePath}v2/guide/`;
const issueUrl = "https://github.com/hara-lang/visual-language/issues/91";
const localNav = [
  { href: "#overview", label: "Overview" },
  { href: "#benchmarks", label: "Benchmarks" },
  { href: "#compatibility", label: "Compatibility" },
  { href: "#telemetry", label: "Telemetry" },
  { href: "#states", label: "States" },
  { href: "#adoption", label: "Adoption" }
];
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="description" content="The Hara v2 data-visualisation guide for benchmark comparisons, confidence, package compatibility, runtime telemetry, missing evidence, accessible tables and downstream adoption." />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="Hara Visual Language" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Hara v2 data visualisation and evidence graphics" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="Accessible evidence graphics with visible units, baselines, uncertainty, revisions and textual alternatives." />
    <meta property="og:url" content={pageUrl} />
    <meta property="og:image" content={socialImage} />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <meta name="twitter:title" content="Hara v2 data visualisation" />
    <meta name="twitter:description" content="Benchmark, compatibility and runtime evidence patterns for Hara products." />
    <meta name="twitter:image" content={socialImage} />
    <link rel="canonical" href={pageUrl} />
    <link rel="icon" href={`${basePath}hara-logo.svg`} type="image/svg+xml" />
    <title>Hara v2 data visualisation and evidence graphics</title>
  </head>
  <body class="hara-v2 hara-v2-data-guide">
    <CatalogueHeader basePath={basePath} activePath="/v2/data/" label="Data visualisation guide">
      <a slot="route-actions" href="#benchmarks">Inspect evidence graphics</a>
    </CatalogueHeader>

    <nav class="data-guide-local-nav" aria-label="Data visualisation guide sections">
      <span>Data</span>
      <div>{localNav.map((item) => <a href={item.href}>{item.label}</a>)}</div>
      <a href={issueUrl}>Issue 91 ↗</a>
    </nav>

    <main class="data-guide-main">
      <aside class="data-guide-fixture-notice" role="note">
        <strong>{dataVisualisationFixtureNotice.label}</strong>
        <span>{dataVisualisationFixtureNotice.summary}</span>
        <code>{dataVisualisationFixtureNotice.id} · {dataVisualisationFixtureNotice.sourceRevision}</code>
      </aside>

      <section class="data-guide-hero" id="overview" aria-labelledby="data-guide-title">
        <div>
          <p class="hara-v2-kicker">Issue 91 · evidence before decoration</p>
          <h1 id="data-guide-title">Show what was measured, what is uncertain, and what cannot be compared.</h1>
          <p>Hara products need one accessible visual grammar for benchmark evidence, package compatibility and runtime observations. The guide keeps scales, units, baselines, confidence, source revision and methodology visible while products retain authority over the underlying facts.</p>
          <div class="data-guide-hero-actions"><a href="#benchmarks">Compare benchmark evidence</a><a href="#compatibility">Inspect compatibility states</a><a href="#telemetry">Read a runtime sequence</a></div>
        </div>
        <aside class="data-guide-hero-ledger" aria-label="Data visualisation fixture summary">
          <header><span>Guide inventory</span><span class="guide-state" data-tone="signal">Additive v2 grammar</span></header>
          <div><p class="data-guide-mono">v2/data-visualisation@1</p><h2>{dataVisualisationSummary.benchmarkSeries + dataVisualisationSummary.compatibilityPackages + dataVisualisationSummary.runtimeEvents} evidence rows</h2><p>Three realistic Hara reference compositions with accessible tabular alternatives and explicit non-production fixture boundaries.</p><dl><div><dt>Benchmark series</dt><dd>{dataVisualisationSummary.benchmarkSeries}</dd></div><div><dt>Compatibility cells</dt><dd>{dataVisualisationSummary.compatibilityPackages * dataVisualisationSummary.compatibilityTargets}</dd></div><div><dt>Runtime events</dt><dd>{dataVisualisationSummary.runtimeEvents}</dd></div><div><dt>Evidence states</dt><dd>{dataVisualisationSummary.evidenceStates}</dd></div></dl></div>
          <footer><span>No decorative perspective</span><span>Tables and text remain first-class</span></footer>
        </aside>
      </section>

      <DataBenchmarkEvidence />
      <DataCompatibilityEvidence />
      <DataRuntimeTelemetry />
      <DataEvidenceStates />

      <footer class="v2-lab-footer"><span>Hara v2 data visualisation and evidence graphics</span><span><a href={catalogueUrl}>Catalogue home</a> · <a href={guideUrl}>Catalogue guide</a> · <a href={issueUrl}>Issue 91</a> · <a href="https://github.com/hara-lang/visual-language">Source</a></span></footer>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
